        {
          "id": "p8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Philo T. Farnsworth was born in the USA in 1906. As a child, he was very interested in science and electricity and spent a lot of time "
            },
            {
              "t": "blank",
              "id": "b19",
              "number": 19
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " about it. He also won a national "
            },
            {
              "t": "blank",
              "id": "b20",
              "number": 20
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " for young engineers when he was just 13."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "When he was 20, Farnsworth "
            },
            {
              "t": "blank",
              "id": "b21",
              "number": 21
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " his own business. In 1927, he showed everyone his new idea: a "
            },
            {
              "t": "blank",
              "id": "b22",
              "number": 22
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " of sending pictures using electricity. Many other people were working on ideas for a machine to do this, but Farnsworth’s was the first that had no moving parts. In fact, it was the first true electronic TV."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "After many business problems, Farnsworth had success in 1938 when another company "
            },
            {
              "t": "blank",
              "id": "b23",
              "number": 23
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " him $1 million for his idea. He is not very famous these "
            },
            {
              "t": "blank",
              "id": "b24",
              "number": 24
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " but, as the father of electronic television, Farnsworth changed the world."
            }
          ]
        }
